## Exercise 4 — resetting on a key

Edit `ex4/solution.tsx`. A boundary that clears itself when its inputs change.

Export:

```tsx
export class ResettableBoundary extends Component<
  {
    children: ReactNode;
    fallback: ReactNode;
    resetKeys?: unknown[];
  },
  { error: Error | null }
> {}
```

Behaviour:

- catches and renders `fallback` as before;
- while in the error state, if any element of `resetKeys` differs from the
  previous render's, clear the error and render `children` again;
- comparison is element-wise with `Object.is`, and a length change also counts;
- when there is no error, changing `resetKeys` does nothing;
- `resetKeys` may be omitted entirely.

The gate renders `<ResettableBoundary resetKeys={[userId]}>` around a child that
throws for `userId === "bad"`, asserts the fallback, then re-renders with
`userId="good"` and asserts the child is back. It also re-renders several times
with the *same* `userId` and asserts the fallback did not clear.

