## Exercise 3 — read all, then write all

Edit `ex3/solution.tsx`. The stub forces a synchronous layout once per row.

Export:

```tsx
export function EqualiseRows(props: {
  rows: { id: string; text: string }[];
  onLayoutRead?: () => void;
}): ReactElement;
```

Behaviour: after render, every row's inline `height` is set to the tallest
row's natural height, so the rows line up.

Requirements:

- measure each row's `offsetHeight`, find the maximum, then write that height to
  every row;
- **all reads must happen before any write** — the gate counts forced layouts by
  instrumenting the `offsetHeight` getter and the style setter, and fails if a
  read follows a write within one pass;
- call `onLayoutRead` once per measured row so the gate can count;
- re-measure when `rows` changes, and clear the inline height before measuring
  so the previous equalisation does not become the new measurement.

```
uv run dojo test react v3rc04_animation_layout ex3
```

references.solution.tsx:
// v3rc04_animation_layout / ex3 - reference solution.
import { useLayoutEffect, useRef } from "react";
import type { ReactElement } from "react";

export function EqualiseRows({
  rows,
  onLayoutRead,
}: {
  rows: { id: string; text: string }[];
  onLayoutRead?: () => void;
}): ReactElement {
  const refs = useRef<(HTMLLIElement | null)[]>([]);

  useLayoutEffect(() => {
    const nodes = refs.current.filter((n): n is HTMLLIElement => n !== null);
    if (nodes.length === 0) return;

    // Pass 1 - writes only. Clearing first means we measure natural height,
    // not last cycle's equalised height, so rows can shrink as well as grow.
    for (const node of nodes) node.style.height = "";

    // Pass 2 - reads only. One forced layout for the whole batch.
    const heights = nodes.map((node) => {
      onLayoutRead?.();
      return node.offsetHeight;
    });

    // Pass 3 - writes only. No read follows, so nothing is forced again.
    const tallest = Math.max(...heights);
    for (const node of nodes) node.style.height = `${tallest}px`;
  }, [rows, onLayoutRead]);

  return (
    <ul>
      {rows.map((row, index) => (
        <li
          key={row.id}
          ref={(node) => {
            refs.current[index] = node;
          }}
        >
          {row.text}
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  );
}

