## Challenge — the accordion

Edit `challenge/solution.tsx`. Animate a panel open and closed when its height
is unknown.

Export:

```tsx
export function Accordion(props: {
  sections: { id: string; title: string; body: ReactNode }[];
  durationMs?: number;
}): ReactElement;
```

Requirements:

- one `<button type="button" aria-expanded aria-controls>` per section and one
  panel per section, with the disclosure semantics from the accessibility
  sector;
- opening and closing animates the panel's height over `durationMs`
  (default `220`), even though the content's height is not known in advance and
  differs per section;
- during the animation the panel must not clip its content incorrectly or
  produce a scrollbar flash;
- after opening completes, the panel must be able to grow if its content grows
  — so it must not be left with a fixed pixel height;
- a section closed mid-open animation reverses smoothly from its current height,
  not from its full height;
- under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`, the panel opens and closes instantly
  with no height animation;
- collapsed panels' content must not be rendered.

Honest difficulty note: `height: auto` is not an animatable value, and the three
common workarounds each fail differently. Pick one and be able to say what its
failure mode is.

