Requirements:

- `LazySettings` is created **once**, at module scope, with
  `lazy(() => import("./settings-page"))`;
- `RequireAuth` renders `children` when `user` is not null;
- when `user` is null it renders `<p role="status">Redirecting…</p>` **and
  nothing else** — the protected children must never be created, never mount,
  and never run an effect;
- the actual `history.replaceState(null, "", redirectTo)` and the `onRedirect`
  call happen in an effect, once per transition into the blocked state;
- `SettingsRoute` composes them with a `Suspense` whose fallback is
  `<p role="status">Loading settings…</p>`, positioned so the fallback shows
  only for an authorised user.

The gate mounts `SettingsRoute` with `user: null` and asserts the settings
module's import function was never called and no effect from the page ran; then
mounts with a user and asserts the loading fallback, then the page.

