```

Requirements:

- `begin()` records a mark named `${name}:start` immediately;
- after the browser has **painted** the resulting update, it records
  `${name}:end` and creates a measure named `name` spanning the two;
- the measure must be readable afterwards via
  `performance.getEntriesByName(name, "measure")`;
- `begin()` called twice before the first completes must not produce a
  mismatched measure — the second call supersedes the first;
- marks and measures are cleared for that name before each new interaction, so
  the buffer does not grow without bound;
- `FilterPanel` calls `begin()` in its select's change handler and reports the
  resulting duration through `onMeasure`.

The gate patches `requestAnimationFrame` to run callbacks synchronously, fires a
change, and asserts a measure named `filter` exists with a non-negative
duration, and that firing twice rapidly leaves exactly one measure.

```
uv run dojo test react v3rc07_profiling_perf ex3
```

exercises.hints:
## Hint 1

`performance.mark(name)` stamps a moment. `performance.measure(name, start, end)`
creates a span between two marks that shows up in the Performance panel's
timings track and in `PerformanceObserver`. Three calls, and your interaction is
named in the same timeline as the browser's own work.

## Hint 2

"After paint" is the interesting requirement. A `requestAnimationFrame` callback
runs *before* the paint of that frame, so a single one is too early. The idiom
is two nested ones — the inner callback runs on the next frame, by which time
the previous frame has been painted:

```tsx
requestAnimationFrame(() => {
  requestAnimationFrame(() => {
    performance.mark(`${name}:end`);
    performance.measure(name, `${name}:start`, `${name}:end`);
  });
});
```

## Hint 3

For the superseding rule, hold the pending frame id in a ref and cancel it at
the start of `begin()`. Then clear the old marks with
`performance.clearMarks(...)` and `performance.clearMeasures(name)` so the
second interaction does not measure from the first one's start mark — which
would report a duration including the user's thinking time.

references.solution.tsx:
// v3rc07_profiling_perf / ex3 - reference solution.
import { useCallback, useEffect, useRef } from "react";
import type { ReactElement } from "react";

export function useInteractionTiming(name: string) {
  const frameRef = useRef<number | null>(null);
  const startMark = `${name}:start`;
  const endMark = `${name}:end`;

  useEffect(
    () => () => {
      if (frameRef.current !== null) cancelAnimationFrame(frameRef.current);
    },
    []
  );

  const begin = useCallback(() => {
    // Supersede any in-flight measurement, and clear its marks, or the next
    // measure would span from the previous interaction's start - reporting the
    // user's thinking time as render cost.
    if (frameRef.current !== null) cancelAnimationFrame(frameRef.current);
    performance.clearMarks(startMark);
    performance.clearMarks(endMark);
    performance.clearMeasures(name);

    performance.mark(startMark);

    // Two nested frames: a requestAnimationFrame callback runs BEFORE that
    // frame's paint, so the inner callback is the first moment the previous
    // frame is on screen. Measuring to the end of the handler instead would
    // exclude render, commit, layout and paint - most of what the user waits
    // for.
    frameRef.current = requestAnimationFrame(() => {
      frameRef.current = requestAnimationFrame(() => {
        frameRef.current = null;
        performance.mark(endMark);
        performance.measure(name, startMark, endMark);
      });
    });
  }, [name, startMark, endMark]);

  return { begin };
}

export function FilterPanel({
  options,
  onMeasure,
}: {
  options: string[];
  onMeasure?: (durationMs: number) => void;
}): ReactElement {
  const { begin } = useInteractionTiming("filter");

  return (
    <select
      aria-label="Filter"
      onChange={() => {
        begin();
        // Read the measure back on a later frame; getEntriesByName returns the
        // measures created above.
        requestAnimationFrame(() =>
          requestAnimationFrame(() => {
            const entries = performance.getEntriesByName("filter", "measure");
            const last = entries[entries.length - 1];
            if (last) onMeasure?.(last.duration);
          })
        );
      }}
    >
      {options.map((option) => (
        <option key={option} value={option}>
          {option}
        </option>
      ))}
    </select>
  );
}

