## Exercise 1 — a scale you cannot escape

Edit `ex1/solution.tsx`. Make an off-scale value a compile error.

Export:

```tsx
export const SPACE: readonly ["0", "4px", "8px", "12px", "16px", "24px", "32px", "48px", "64px"];
export type SpaceStep = 0 | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5 | 6 | 7 | 8;

export function Box(props: {
  padding?: SpaceStep;
  paddingX?: SpaceStep;
  gap?: SpaceStep;
  unsafeStyle?: CSSProperties;
  children?: ReactNode;
}): ReactElement;
```

Requirements:

- `padding` sets `padding` to `var(--space-N)`; `paddingX` sets
  `padding-inline`, and when both are given `paddingX` wins on the inline axis;
- `gap` sets `gap`, and the box is `display: flex` only when `gap` is supplied —
  a `Box` with no `gap` must not change its children's layout;
- these must be **type errors**: `padding={13}`, `padding="16px"`,
  `padding={-1}`;
- `unsafeStyle` is the deliberate escape hatch: it is merged **after** the token
  styles so it can override them, and its name is chosen so it is greppable;
- omitted props emit no CSS property at all — no `padding: undefined`, no
  `padding: var(--space-undefined)`.

The gate renders `<Box padding={4} gap={2}>` and asserts the inline style is
exactly `{ padding: "var(--space-4)", gap: "var(--space-2)", display: "flex" }`,
then type-checks a file containing `<Box padding={13} />` and asserts it fails.

```
uv run dojo test react v3rc08_design_systems_theming ex1
```

references.solution.tsx:
// v3rc08_design_systems_theming / ex1 - reference solution.
import type { CSSProperties, ReactElement, ReactNode } from "react";

export const SPACE = [
  "0",
  "4px",
  "8px",
  "12px",
  "16px",
  "24px",
  "32px",
  "48px",
  "64px",
] as const;

// The enforcement is the type. A runtime warning would fire in a browser
// somebody has to open; this fires in the editor before the commit.
export type SpaceStep = 0 | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5 | 6 | 7 | 8;

export function Box({
  padding,
  paddingX,
  gap,
  unsafeStyle,
  children,
}: {
  padding?: SpaceStep;
  paddingX?: SpaceStep;
  gap?: SpaceStep;
  // Named to be greppable: a design system with no way out gets forked, and one
  // whose way out is called `style` gets used for everything.
  unsafeStyle?: CSSProperties;
  children?: ReactNode;
}): ReactElement {
  const style: CSSProperties = {
    // var(), not the literal value: the component never learns what --space-4
    // is, so a theme can change the whole scale without touching components.
    ...(padding !== undefined ? { padding: `var(--space-${padding})` } : null),
    // After `padding`, so it wins on the inline axis.
    ...(paddingX !== undefined
      ? { paddingInline: `var(--space-${paddingX})` }
      : null),
    // display: flex only when gap is asked for - otherwise a plain Box would
    // silently change its children's layout.
    ...(gap !== undefined
      ? { gap: `var(--space-${gap})`, display: "flex" }
      : null),
    // Last, so the escape hatch can override anything above it.
    ...unsafeStyle,
  };

  return <div style={style}>{children}</div>;
}

