Requirements:

- `CARD_CSS` is a CSS string that establishes a container on `.card-host`
  (`container-type: inline-size`) and, inside `@container (min-width: 400px)`,
  switches `.card` from a vertical to a horizontal layout;
- `MediaCard` renders `<div class="card-host"><div class="card">…` so the same
  card is narrow in a sidebar and wide in a main column **with no props and no
  measurement**;
- `Stack` renders a vertical flex column with `gap: var(--space-N)` and no
  margins anywhere;
- `Cluster` renders a horizontal, wrapping flex row with the same gap treatment;
- neither primitive sets any margin, and `MediaCard` sets none either — all
  spacing comes from the primitives' `gap`;
- `Stack`'s `as` prop defaults to `div`, and when it is `ul` the children are
  expected to be `li`s — it must not add wrappers.

The gate parses `CARD_CSS` and asserts it contains a `container-type` and an
`@container` rule, renders `MediaCard` and asserts no element in it has a
non-zero margin in its inline style, and checks `Stack`/`Cluster` computed
`flex-direction`.

